<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ndebele Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ndebele</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ndebele Kingdom was a state established by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mzilikazi">Mzilikazi</a> on the south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a> around 1840. Its arrival from the south completed the military occupation of the former heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a>. The kingdom drew in part on earlier plateau political precedents and later fell to British colonial forces in the 1890s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ndebele Kingdom" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scanned by Ulamm, modified by Fvasconcellos · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matabeleland.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
